Patch summary:
On a host that samples ASTC natively with optimal tiling but not linear
tiling (Honeykrisp on Apple silicon), create optimal-tiled ASTC images
natively and emulate only linear-tiled ones. Upstream emulates every ASTC
image there (4e8e7ad8: optimal-only ASTC "is not enough to run Android
apps"), which gives each texture a decompressed RGBA8 copy in the guest's
memory, 4-16x its compressed size. The guest still sees linear-tiled ASTC
support, from emulation: format properties report the host's native
optimal-tiling features and emulation's linear-tiling features, image
format queries and image creation decide per tiling, and the host device
keeps its ASTC feature enabled. Hosts without native ASTC emulate every
ASTC image as before; hosts with full support do not emulate.

